12u-01  THE d SHELL AT THE 37.1% ROW
  (3,3,1,3,1)        l_max = 1   n_max - 1 = 2   admits l = 2 (a d subshell): False
  (4,4,1,6,1)        l_max = 1   n_max - 1 = 3   admits l = 2 (a d subshell): False
  (4,4,2,6,2)        l_max = 2   n_max - 1 = 3   admits l = 2 (a d subshell): True
  (5,5,2,6,2)        l_max = 2   n_max - 1 = 4   admits l = 2 (a d subshell): True
  The section reads: "Once the d shell is open the share sits at 37-38%".
  The first row admitting l = 2 is (4,4,2,6,2), at 37.7%.
  The 37.1% row is (4,4,1,6,1) -- l_max = 1, the SAME cap as the 63.2% row it is
  contrasted with.  What changes between those two rows is n, e and k, not l.
  CONFIRMED: the d shell is absent at the 37.1% row.

12u-02  THE TWO RANGES THE SENTENCE JOINS
  "moves by less than a point across a fiftyfold growth in cells"
  the fiftyfold growth is 1,654 -> 83,543 cells = 50.5x,
    and across it the share moves 25.3 points (63.2% -> 37.9%).
  the range over which it moves less than a point is 19,433 -> 83,543 = 4.3x,
    over which it moves 0.8 points (37.1% -> 37.9%).
  CONFIRMED: one clause's growth belongs to the other clause's range.

